# R75: the one way a scratch address reaches a kosh unseen - through a prakriya that returns it.
# A KNOWN LIMIT, pinned: this compiles, and reads through the kept address. Up to v318 it printed 99 - the NEXT
# block's data. From v320 (R175, R176) a block's memory is zeroed when the block is left, so it prints 0. The address is
# still dangling: had the read come while the second block was alive, it would have read that block's data.
# A future check that refuses it will fail this test; that is the point.
prakriya adr(p)
    nivartanam p
mukhya()
    kosh k[1]
    mandapa
        vitti buf = nirmmita(64)
        buf[0] = 42
        kosh_push(k, adr(buf))
    mandapa
        vitti other = nirmmita(64)
        other[0] = 99
    vitti p = k[0]
    likha(p[0], "\n")
